"use strict";(self.webpackChunkkeldev=self.webpackChunkkeldev||[]).push([[4328],{4371:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"archive":{"blogPosts":[{"id":"/2026/08/20/free-radio-foobar","metadata":{"permalink":"/thoughts/2026/08/20/free-radio-foobar","source":"@site/thoughts/2026/08/20-free-radio-foobar.mdx","title":"free-radio-foobar","description":"I recently discovered you can set up a fun, customizable, capable internet radio listening experience without purchasing anything.","date":"2026-08-20T18:53:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Music","permalink":"/thoughts/tags/music","description":"Posts about music."},{"inline":false,"label":"Software","permalink":"/thoughts/tags/software","description":"Posts about software, but not necessarily technical posts."},{"inline":false,"label":"Media","permalink":"/thoughts/tags/media","description":"Posts about media (music, games, books, etc.)."}],"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"date":"2026-08-20T18:53","tags":["music","software","media"]},"unlisted":false},"content":"I recently discovered you can set up a fun, customizable, capable internet radio listening experience without purchasing anything.\\n\\n<a class=\\"zoomable\\" href=\\"https://assets.keldev.net/thoughts/2026/08/20/foobar2000-radio-kexp.gif\\" target=\\"blank\\"><img decoding=\\"async\\" loading=\\"lazy\\" alt=\\".gif of my foobar2000 setup tuned to KEXP.\\" class=\\"img_ev3q\\" src=\\"https://assets.keldev.net/thoughts/2026/08/20/foobar2000-radio-kexp.gif\\"/></a>\\n\\nThe program is [foobar2000](https://www.foobar2000.org/). It\'s classic freeware.\\nI\'d heard of it before but I haven\'t maintained a library of local music files in like 10 years, so I never had\\nmuch reason to download it until recently when I wanted to try [the new album from King Gizzard & The Lizard Wizard](https://kinggizzard.bandcamp.com/album/alien-metal).\\nThey [removed their catalog from Spotify](https://brobible.com/culture/article/australian-psychedelic-rock-gods-king-gizzard-appear-to-be-nuking-their-catalog-from-spotify/) a while back,\\nbut all their albums are available at \\"name your price\\" on Bandcamp.\\n\\nI wanted a program that wasn\'t just Windows Media Player, and it turns out [VLC](https://www.videolan.org/vlc/index.html) (which I already use for video)\\ndoesn\'t do gapless playback for audio. Figured this is my chance to try out foobar.\\n\\nAnd, well, it\'s really cool! And it does radio too.\\n\\nIt\'s ancient and modular. The standard version of the program is a collection of built-in components,\\nand you can add whatever [community-made components](https://www.foobar2000.org/components/by+date) you\\nwant on top of that. You can go fully custom for themes/skins/icons and layout as well.\\n\\n<a class=\\"zoomable\\" href=\\"https://assets.keldev.net/thoughts/2026/08/20/foobar2000-radio-layout.png\\" target=\\"blank\\"><img decoding=\\"async\\" loading=\\"lazy\\" alt=\\"Screenshot of my foobar2000 setup with all UI panels labeled.\\" class=\\"img_ev3q\\" src=\\"https://assets.keldev.net/thoughts/2026/08/20/foobar2000-radio-layout.png\\"/></a>\\nI set mine up so I could throw it on my portrait monitor. Here are my UI components:\\n1. **Album List**. Built-in. Shows local media. I pointed mine at the 4 KGLW albums I downloaded.\\n2. **Selection Properties**. Built-in. Metadata for the \\"selected\\" track. When radio is playing this shows info about the current station.\\n3. **Playlist View**. Built-in. Basic track-by-track view of your current playlist, or artist/trackname info for the current radio track.\\n4. **OpenLyrics Panel**. [Community-made.](https://www.foobar2000.org/components/view/foo_openlyrics) Uses the current track name and artist info to search a few online sources for lyrics. Depending on source this can also time the display to auto-scroll and highlight lyrics as the song progresses. Mine favors Genius, and I\'ve turned off scrolling.\\n5. **Internet Radio**. Built-in. Lets you search, bookmark, and tune in to whatever public internet radio stations you want. Right now I have [KEXP](https://kexp.org/), NPR,\\nand WBEZ Chicago.\\n6. **Artwork Display**. [Community-made.](https://github.com/jame25/foo_artwork) Uses the current track name and artist info to search online sources for album artwork, when local artwork isn\'t found. I also have the built-in EQ component on another tab here.\\n7. **Spectrogram**, **Oscilloscope**, and **Spectrum Analyzer**. All built-in. The Spectrogram is using the 2-channel view and has custom orange coloring. The Oscilloscope is downmixing to mono, with a 200ms curve duration. Spectrum analyzer uses 160 bands.\\n\\nI\'ve also set up a [community-made](https://github.com/gix/foo_scrobble) scrobbling component\\nfor [LastFM](https://www.last.fm/user/A_Univrsal_Sigh). It sets \\"now playing\\" for radio but does not save\\nthe scrobbles. Listens from local files are scrobbled. I only want my more intentional listening tracked, but\\ndon\'t mind sharing what I\'ve got playing on the radio, so this does exactly that.\\n\\nEnd result is a neat display I leave off to the side, with fun visualizers, lyrics, art, and a human connection to \\nthe live DJs on KEXP, all for free.\\n\\nThis actually reminded me how much the Spotify UX irritates me. I would love to stare at a spectrogram or to be able to change\\nthe source that Spotify is using for lyrics, or replace album artwork.. Or listen without having to see all the\\ncontent that Spotify\'s suggestion algorithms are serving me today if I don\'t want to. Or rearrange the UI panels.\\nRemove stuff I don\'t want to see. Change colors.\\n\\nBasically I would love to be able to pipe my Spotify streaming through foobar2000.\\n\\n[Alas.](https://github.com/TheQwertiest/foo_spotify/issues/68) This only _used to be_ possible:\\n> Spotify deprecated the library that was used to implement playback in this component.  \\n> There are no viable Windows alternatives that could be used to replace it, hence this project is suspended until such alternative appears.\\n\\nLive radio has been fun to rediscover though. Give it a try!"}]}}')}}]);